{
  "mn111:0.1": "Middle Discourses 111 ",
  "mn111:0.2": "One by One ",
  "mn111:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn111:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn111:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn111:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn111:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn111:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn111:2.1": "“Sāriputta is astute, mendicants. ",
  "mn111:2.2": "He has great wisdom, ",
  "mn111:2.3": "widespread wisdom, ",
  "mn111:2.4": "laughing wisdom, ",
  "mn111:2.5": "swift wisdom, ",
  "mn111:2.6": "sharp wisdom, ",
  "mn111:2.7": "and penetrating wisdom. ",
  "mn111:2.8": "For a fortnight he practiced discernment of phenomena one by one. ",
  "mn111:2.9": "And this is how he did it. ",
  "mn111:3.1": "Quite secluded from sensual pleasures, secluded from unskillful qualities, he entered and remained in the first absorption, which has the rapture and bliss born of seclusion, while placing the mind and keeping it connected. ",
  "mn111:4.1": "And he distinguished the phenomena of the first absorption one by one: placing and keeping and rapture and bliss and unification of mind; contact, feeling, perception, intention, mind, enthusiasm, decision, energy, mindfulness, equanimity, and application of mind. ",
  "mn111:4.2": "He knew those phenomena as they arose, as they remained, and as they went away. ",
  "mn111:4.3": "He understood: ",
  "mn111:4.4": "‘So it seems that thes